{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"check\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"unit-C1-recovery-adopts-committed-vector\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Strengthened scenario for the C1 obligation: the committed record the recovering replica ignores is no longer installed directly. The harness drives a real proposal on instance (1,0) - handlePropose, the PreAccept round and the fast-path commit broadcast - with the commit delivered only to replica 2, so it produces a legal history in which the owner holds the instance COMMITTED with a real PUT and another replica installed that commit. The recovering replica 0 (a default record) then runs recovery and the same divergence follows: the COMMITTED reply is skipped, the accept round commits a NOOP vector, and the propagation and applied-state observations differ. This removes the prepared-record limitation the earlier reviews recorded. The local construction run shows leader_status 4 and third_status 4 for the proposal, then adopted_committed false, vectors_match false, all_committed_match false and applied_match false.\\\",\n \\\"plan_path\\\":\\\"plan-recovery-divergence.json\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"explore_fullhistory_test.go\\\",\\\"files\\\":{}}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-c1-fullhistory.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-c1-fullhistory.json 2>&1 | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
